		(uuid "65f4bc33-b03a-5212-9c3c-1dbb2abf5850")
	)
	(text "TPS3850G33: 3V3 window +/-4 %, tRST 200 ms (CRST open). WDI falling edge every 10.35-165.8 ms\n(CWD 10k, SET0 0, SET1 1), else WDO pulses SYS_RST_N low 200 ms. Wired-AND with CTRL XRSn\n(CTRL 10k + 10 nF; 100k here keeps the node defined without CTRL). SET0 / SET1 from the service jumper."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 214.644 66.9 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.1 1.1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "73b547b5-5298-5311-9469-7125d9f06ec1")
	)
	(text "BOTH CHANNELS: AUX-HV SOURCE INHIBIT (D-022: AUX-HV ALONE NEVER RUNS POWER)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 14 102.604 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "84ca592f-1d5c-5027-bae5-4db4649a7ae2")
	)
	(text "J802 service jumper (programming / debug only; no shunt fitted in service). Fitted: SVC_N = 0 ->\nSET1 = 0 and, through Q, SET0 = 1 -> TPS3850 watchdog DISABLED (table 6.6); BAT54C pulls TEST_A_N and\nTEST_B_N low -> both channels held tripped: GATE_EN, CHB_OK, FLT_LATCH_N = 0, 24V_DO and +24V_GD off. The\nmodule cannot look healthy or run power; CTRL (+24V) stays powered for programming. SVC_N -> expander 2.\nFIRMWARE: first WDI falling edge <= 150 ms after EVERY XRSn release (tWDU min 165.8 ms), then every\n10.35-165.8 ms (closed window 10.35 ms max). Report service mode (SVC_RB = 0) and refuse FLT_CLR."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 548.78 90.104 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.1 1.1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "8542acb8-7ee9-5136-9248-e4f4ef3bdf33")
	)
	(text "CHANNEL A INPUT: SPARE TRIP LOOP J801"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 370.844 19 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "8e15a620-d16d-52e6-b6d1-1eaf3842cffb")
	)
	(text "CHANNEL B, separate parts. U811: RST_B = Schmitt(SYS_RST_N);  U812: NO_TRIP_B = ESTOP_B_OK & RST_B & TEST_B_N\nU813 D-FF: CLR = NO_TRIP_B (dominant), D = 1, CLK = FLT_CLR     U814: CHB_OK = LATCH_B_OK & NO_TRIP_B\nCHB_OK -> +24V_GD switch (gate-drive bias), 24V_DO switch B, and via U815 to CTRL (ANDed into every EN pair).\n  any B input 0 -> Q_B 0 -> +24V_GD off, switch B off, CHB_OK 0;  re-arm only by a FLT_CLR edge with B healthy\n24V_DO = switch A AND switch B in series. Gate off = GATE_EN 0 (A) OR +24V_GD off (B).\nCHB_OK_L has 10k to GND (two SHDN pull-ups x 10 uA -> 0.2 V < 0.8 V): unpowered driver or dead 3V3 = OFF."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 14 283.584 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.1 1.1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "e106fcc3-63a3-5fde-945b-099100ab4bf5")
	)
	(text "AUX_EN (LM74800 EN/UVLO, sheet 01) -> 100k / (200k || 200k) -> TPS3700 INB-: AUX_INH_N low while AUX_EN >\n0.72-0.82 V, i.e. before the LM74800 can enable (V(UVLOR) >= 1.195 V) and until it is back in shutdown\n(priority detector VOL <= 0.25 V). BAT54C pulls TEST_A_N and TEST_B_N low: both channels trip and LATCH\n(+24V_GD, 24V_DO off; GATE_EN, CHB_OK 0); FAN_ON = FAN_EN AND AUX_INH_N (sheet 10). No firmware in the path.\nCabinet back: fans may restart, power needs FLT_CLR. AUX-HV absent: AUX_EN = 0, no inhibit (cabinet-only\nmodules arm normally). Hot-plugged AUX-HV: the detector OUTA hold-off keeps AUX_EN <= 0.57 V.\nFirmware reads AUX_INH_RB (expander 2 GPB5, 0 = AUX-HV is the source, power inhibited). Self-test: AUX_TEST\n(GPB6) high -> AUX_INH_RB 0, both channels trip, fans off; release, FLT_CLR.\nAUX-HV load with the branches off: 27.8 W worst case <= 30 W (13.9 W of it the port board for <= 200 s)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 14 189.428 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.1 1.1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "e23bb9c3-b2c1-504a-a157-09b5df03def4")
	)
	(text "CHANNEL A LATCH"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 190.032 102.604 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "f2f2e672-db22-52e1-95d3-804085f18bd7")
	)
	(text "CHANNEL A (1 = healthy). U806: FIELD_A_OK = ESTOP_A_OK & UV_OK & TEST_A_N;  U805: RST_A = Schmitt(SYS_RST_N)\nU807: NO_TRIP_A = FIELD_A_OK & TRIP_OK & RST_A     U808 D-FF: CLR = NO_TRIP_A (dominant), D = 1, CLK = FLT_CLR\nU809: GATE_EN = LATCH_A_OK & NO_TRIP_A -> CTRL EN pairs     U810: DO_PWR_EN = LATCH_A_OK & NO_TRIP_A -> 24V_DO switch A\n  any A input 0            -> NO_TRIP_A 0 -> Q_A 0 at once -> GATE_EN 0, switch A off, FLT_LATCH_N 0\n  inputs back, FLT_CLR held -> stays latched (no automatic restart)\n  all inputs 1, FLT_CLR rise -> Q_A 1 -> GATE_EN 1, switch A on;  input still 0 at the edge -> stays tripped\n  power-up: TPS3850 holds SYS_RST_N low 200 ms -> both latches start tripped\nDO_PWR_EN has 10k to GND: an unpowered gate or a dead 3V3 leaves switch A OFF (its SHDN pull-up is <= 10 uA)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 190.032 190.264 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.1 1.1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "f57d4af7-ccfa-5e65-8187-5bb325178c5a")
	)
	(text "E-STOP STATUS, LEDS AND SINGLE-FAULT ANALYSIS"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
